+# Fix for Multi-line Help Text in Fish Shell Completion
+
+## Problem
+Multi-line help text in Click commands was causing errors during fish shell completion. When help text contained literal newlines (e.g., `help="\b\nAttachment with explicit mimetype,\n--at image.jpg image/jpeg"`), the fish completion script would fail to parse the completion data correctly.
+
+## Root Cause
+The fish shell completion script processes each completion item by splitting on newlines, but multi-line help text containing literal newlines would corrupt this parsing process.
+
+## Solution
+The FishComplete.format_completion method in Click already implements proper escaping of newlines. When a CompletionItem has help text with newlines:
+
+1. The newline characters in both `value` and `help` fields are replaced with the two-character escape sequence `\n`
+2. This ensures that when fish shell processes the completion data, the escaped newlines round-trip correctly without breaking the parsing
+
+## Implementation
+The fix was implemented in version 8.4.0 in `src/click/shell_completion.py`:
+
+```python
+def format_completion(self, item: CompletionItem) -> str:
+    """
+    .. versionchanged:: 8.4.0
+        Escape newlines in value and help to fix completion errors with
+        multi-line help strings.
+    """
+    # The fish completion script splits each response line on literal
+    # newlines, so any newline in the value or help would corrupt the
+    # frame. Replace them with the two-character escape "\n" so the text
+    # round-trips through fish without breaking the format. The "_"
+    # sentinel for missing help mirrors :class:`ZshComplete`.
+    help_ = item.help or "_"
+    value = item.value.replace("\n", r"\n")
+    help_escaped = help_.replace("\n", r"\n")
+    return f"{item.type}\n{value}\n{help_escaped}"
+```
+
+This ensures that multi-line help text is properly escaped for fish shell completion and will display correctly in the completion suggestions.
